***************************************************************** 2831 1451
 New evaluation above the resonance region, below 20 MeV          2831 1451
                                        T. Kawano (LANL) Oct 2012 2831 1451
                                                                  2831 1451
   Many of sections in MF=3,4,6,12, and 14 were updated based     2831 1451
on the CoH3 calculations. We preserved the old document in MF=1   2831 1451
by D.C. Larson, et al. of ENDF/B-VI for record keeping purpose.   2831 1451
The default claculations fit the avaiable experimental (n,p) and  2831 1451
(n,2n) data reasonably well. Some adjustment to the model         2831 1451
parameters was made. The (n,2p) and (n,p alpha) cross sections    2831 1451
were newly evaluated.                                             2831 1451
                                                                  2831 1451
   Above 20MeV, the cross sections are the same as                2831 1451
ENDF/B-VII.1 (LA150).                                             2831 1451
                                                                  2831 1451
 MF  2: Resonance region                                          2831 1451
   MT 151: The resonance parameters are the same as               2831 1451
      in ENDF/B-VII.1, evaluated at ORNL. See text below.         2831 1451
                                                                  2831 1451
 MF  3: Neutron cross sections                                    2831 1451
   MT   1: Total cross section, same as ENDF/B-VII.1.             2831 1451
   MT   4: Total inelastic scattering cross section               2831 1451
      sum of MT 51 - 91.                                          2831 1451
   MT  16: (n,2n) cross section                                   2831 1451
      Calculated with the CoH3 code.                              2831 1451
      The AMS Data by Wallner et al. 2006 have two points:        2831 1451
      17 and 19 MeV. The 19-MeV data point was not able to        2831 1451
      reprodue with the model calculation.                        2831 1451
   MT  22: (n,na) cross section                                   2831 1451
      Calculated with the CoH3 code.                              2831 1451
   MT  28: (n,np) cross section                                   2831 1451
      Calculated with the CoH3 code.                              2831 1451
   MT  51 - 91: (n,n') cross section                              2831 1451
      Calculated with the CoH3 code.                              2831 1451
      DWBA cross sections were given to                           2831 1451
      MT = 51, 54, 57, 63, and 78                                 2831 1451
   MT 102: (n,gamma) cross section                                2831 1451
      Calculated with the CoH3 code. The model parameters         2831 1451
      were adjusted to available experimental data and            2831 1451
      the evaluated MACS. However the new calculation does not    2831 1451
      change the MACS because the resonance boundary is 800 keV.  2831 1451
   MT 103: (n,p) cross section                                    2831 1451
      Calculated with the CoH3 code.                              2831 1451
      The excitation function was modified below                  2831 1451
      12 MeV for better agreement with the data of Vonach 1989,   2831 1451
      Wagner 1991, and Sudar 1991.                                2831 1451
   MT 104: (n,d) cross section                                    2831 1451
      Calculated with the CoH3 code.                              2831 1451
      The calculation does not fit to the data of Grimes 1979     2831 1451
      nor Graham 1987.                                            2831 1451
   MT 105: (n,t) cross section                                    2831 1451
      Calculated with the CoH3 code.                              2831 1451
   MT 107: (n,a) cross section                                    2831 1451
      Calculated with the CoH3 code.                              2831 1451
   MT 111: (n,2p) cross section                                   2831 1451
      Calculated with the CoH3 code.                              2831 1451
   MT 112: (n,pa) cross section                                   2831 1451
      Calculated with the CoH3 code.                              2831 1451
                                                                  2831 1451
 MF  4 Angular distributions of emitted neutrons                  2831 1451
   MT   2: elastic scattering                                     2831 1451
       0 - 800 keV:                                               2831 1451
          the P1, P2, and P3 were calculated                      2831 1451
          from the resonance parapeters,                          2831 1451
          and Gaussian smoothing applied.                         2831 1451
      800 keV - 20 MeV:                                           2831 1451
