                                                                  2831 1451
 ENDF/B-VI MOD 2 Revision, July 1991, D.C. Larson, C.M. Perey,    2831 1451
                 D.M. Hetrick, and C.Y. Fu (ORNL)                 2831 1451
                                                                  2831 1451
 REVISION 1 CHANGES                                               2831 1451
   The resonance region from 1.E-5 eV to 450 keV has been changed,2831 1451
 based on a SAMMY analysis by F. G. Perey of new 60Ni ORELA data  2831 1451
 up to 100 keV of Harvey, Hill and Perey. This new work reproduces2831 1451
 the thermal cross sections and includes the small resonances     2831 1451
 inadvertently left out in the original file.  No background      2831 1451
 cross sections are required in file 3 in the resonance region.   2831 1451
   Removed elastic transformation matrix.                         2831 1451
                                                                  2831 1451
 **************************************************************** 2831 1451
                                                                  2831 1451
 ENDF/B-VI MOD 1 Evaluation, October 1989, D.C. Larson,           2831 1451
                 C.M. Perey, D.M. Hetrick, and C.Y. Fu (ORNL)     2831 1451
                                                                  2831 1451
   This work employed nuclear model codes including the           2831 1451
 Distorted Wave Born Approximation (DWBA) program DWUCK (1)       2831 1451
 and the Hauser-Feshbach code TNG (2,3,4).  The TNG code provides 2831 1451
 energy and angular distributions of particles emitted in the     2831 1451
 compound and pre-compound reactions, ensures consistency among   2831 1451
 all reactions, and maintains energy balance. Details pertinent   2831 1451
 to the contents of this evaluation and extensive comparisons of  2831 1451
 calculations with experimental data can be found in Hetrick (5). 2831 1451
                                                                  2831 1451
***************************************************************   2831 1451
                                                                  2831 1451
----- DESCRIPTION OF FILES                                        2831 1451
(MF-MT)                                                           2831 1451
  1-451 GENERAL INFORMATION, REFERENCES, AND DEFINITIONS.         2831 1451
  2-151 RESONANCE PARAMETERS -- SEE NEW ORNL EVALUATION ABOVE     2831 1451
  3-1   TOTAL CROSS SECTION -- FROM 450 KEV TO 1611 KEV THE DATA  2831 1451
        OF REF (8) WERE USED.  FROM 1611 KEV TO 20 MEV THE DATA   2831 1451
        OF REF (9) WERE USED.  SEVERAL LOWER RESOLUTION DATA SETS 2831 1451
        WERE ENERGY-BINNED AND CHECKED WITH BINNED DATA FROM 8,9. 2831 1451
  3-2   ELASTIC SCATTERING CROSS SECTIONS WERE OBTAINED BY        2831 1451
        SUBTRACTING THE NONELASTIC FROM THE TOTAL                 2831 1451
  3-3   NONELASTIC CROSS SECTION; SUM OF 3-4, 3-16, 3-22,         2831 1451
        3-28, 3-102, 3-103, 3-104, AND 3-107.                     2831 1451
  3-4   TOTAL INELASTIC CROSS SECTION; SUM OF 3-51, 3-52, ..      2831 1451
        .., 3-61, AND 3-91                                        2831 1451
  3-16  (N,2N) CROSS SECTIONS WERE CALCULATED BY THE TNG          2831 1451
        CODE (2,3,4,5), NO 60NI DATA AVAILABLE.                   2831 1451
  3-22  (N,NA) CROSS SECTIONS WERE CALCULATED BY THE TNG          2831 1451
        CODE (2,3,4,5). NO 60NI DATA AVAILABLE OTHER THAN A EMISS 2831 1451
  3-28  (N,NP) CROSS SECTIONS WERE CALCULATED BY THE TNG          2831 1451
        CODE (2,3,4,5). NO 60NI DATA AVAILABLE OTHER THAN P EMISS 2831 1451
  3-51 TO 3-61 INELASTIC SCATTERING EXCITING LEVELS; RESULTS ARE  2831 1451
        FROM TNG (2,3,4,5) WHICH INCLUDES DIRECT INTERACTION      2831 1451
        CROSS SECTIONS FROM DWUCK (1) CALCULATIONS.  CALCULATIONS 2831 1451
        COMPARED WITH EXTENSIVE EXPERIMENTAL DATA (5).  3-51 CROSS2831 1451
        SECTIONS ABOVE 4.0 MEV ADJUSTED TO BETTER FIT RECENT      2831 1451
        MEASURED DATA.                                            2831 1451
  3-91  INELASTIC SCATTERING EXCITING THE CONTINUUM (TNG          2831 1451
        CALCULATED).                                              2831 1451
  3-102 (N,G) CAPTURE CROSS SECTION TAKEN FROM RESONANCE PARAMETER2831 1451
        FROM 1.E-5 EV TO 450 KEV. TNG CALCULATIONS WERE           2831 1451
        NORMALIZED TO THE AVERAGED CROSS SECTION OBTAINED FROM THE2831 1451
        RESONANCE PARAMETERS FROM 100-450 KEV.  THESE NORMALIZED  2831 1451
        TNG RESULTS WERE USED FROM 450 KEV TO 20 MEV.             2831 1451
  3-103 (N,P) CROSS SECTIONS FOR EN LESS THAN OR EQUAL TO 12 MEV  2831 1451
        WERE TAKEN FROM A CURVE DRAWN THROUGH THE DATA OF VONACH  2831 1451
        ET AL. (10). THIS CURVE WAS CONNECTED TO THE ANL DATA OF  2831 1451
        GREENWOOD (11) FROM 14.5 TO 15.0 MEV. FROM 15.0 TO 20.0   2831 1451
        MEV THE DATA OF PAULSEN AND LISKIEN (12) WERE USED        2831 1451
        AS A GUIDE.  THE NEW DATA BY VONACH ET AL. (10)           2831 1451
        RESULT IN AN INTEGRAL VALUE CLOSE TO THE 2.39 VALUE OF    2831 1451
        MANNHART (13).                                            2831 1451
  3-104 (N,D) CROSS SECTION - ENDF/B-V (14) VALUES WERE NORMALIZED2831 1451
        TO THE DATA OF GRIMES ET AL. (15).                        2831 1451
  3-107 (N,A) CROSS SECTIONS WERE CALCULATED BY THE               2831 1451
        TNG CODE (2,3,4,5). LIMITED DATA OTHER THAN A EMISSION.   2831 1451
  4-2   ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS OF SECONDARY NEUTRONS GIVEN FOR     2831 1451
        ELASTIC SCATTERING ARE FROM ENDF/B-V. AGREE WELL WITH DATA2831 1451
        IF DESIRED, ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS CAN BE CALCULATED BY    2831 1451
        THE USER ON A FINER ENERGY GRID FROM THE R-M RESONANCE    2831 1451
        PARAMETERS IN 2/151.                                      2831 1451
  6-16  (N,2N) REACTION; INCLUDES SIMPLE CONSTANT YIELDS FOR THE  2831 1451
        NEUTRON AND 59NI RESIDUAL, AND ENERGY DEPENDENT YIELD     2831 1451
        BASED ON TNG CALCULATED GAMMA-RAY SPECTRA FOR THE GAMMA   2831 1451
        RAY; TNG CALCULATED NORMALIZED DISTRIBUTIONS ARE GIVEN FOR2831 1451
        EACH PRODUCT (ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS ARE GIVEN ONLY FOR    2831 1451
        THE OUTGOING NEUTRON).  COMPARES WELL WITH N EMISSION DATA2831 1451
        WHEN COMBINED WITH N FROM 6/22, 6/28 AND 6/91.            2831 1451
  6-22  (N,NA)+(N,AN); INCLUDES SIMPLE CONSTANT YIELDS FOR THE    2831 1451
        NEUTRON, ALPHA, AND 56FE RESIDUAL, AND ENERGY DEPENDENT   2831 1451
        YIELD BASED ON TNG CALCULATED GAMMA-RAY SPECTRA FOR THE   2831 1451
        GAMMA RAY; CALCULATED NORMALIZED DISTRIBUTIONS ARE GIVEN  2831 1451
        FOR EACH PRODUCT (ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS ARE GIVEN ONLY    2831 1451
        FOR THE OUTGOING NEUTRON; ISOTROPY IS ASSUMED FOR THE     2831 1451
        ALPHA AND RESIDUAL).                                      2831 1451
  6-28  (N,NP)+(N,PN); INCLUDES SIMPLE CONSTANT YIELDS FOR THE    2831 1451
        NEUTRON, P, AND 59CO RESIDUAL, AND ENERGY DEPENDENT YIELD 2831 1451
        BASED ON TNG CALCULATED GAMMA-RAY SPECTRA FOR THE GAMMA   2831 1451
        RAY; CALCULATED NORMALIZED DISTRIBUTIONS ARE GIVEN FOR    2831 1451
        EACH PRODUCT (ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS ARE GIVEN ONLY FOR    2831 1451
        THE OUTGOING NEUTRON).                                    2831 1451
  6-51 THROUGH 6-61 INELASTIC SCATTERING EXCITING LEVELS; EACH    2831 1451
        SECTION INCLUDES SIMPLE CONSTANT YIELDS FOR THE NEUTRON   2831 1451
        AND 60NI RESIDUAL; ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS ARE GIVEN FOR    2831 1451
        THE OUTGOING NEUTRON (LEGENDRE COEFFICIENTS COMPUTED      2831 1451
        BY DWUCK (1) AND TNG (2,3,4,5)), COMPARED WITH DATA IN (5)2831 1451
  6-91  INELASTIC SCATTERING EXCITING THE CONTINUUM; INCLUDES     2831 1451
        SIMPLE CONSTANT YIELDS FOR THE NEUTRON AND 60NI           2831 1451
        RESIDUAL AND ENERGY DEPENDENT YIELD BASED ON TNG          2831 1451
        CALCULATED GAMMA-RAY SPECTRA FOR THE GAMMA RAY; TNG       2831 1451
        CALCULATED NORMALIZED DISTRIBUTIONS ARE GIVEN             2831 1451
        FOR EACH (ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS ARE GIVEN ONLY FOR THE    2831 1451
        OUTGOING NEUTRON).                                        2831 1451
  6-103 (N,P) REACTION; INCLUDES SIMPLE CONSTANT YIELDS FOR P     2831 1451
        AND 60CO RESIDUAL, AND ENERGY DEPENDENT YIELD BASED       2831 1451
        ON CALCULATED GAMMA-RAY SPECTRA FOR GAMMA RAY;            2831 1451
        CALCULATED NORMALIZED DISTRIBUTIONS ARE GIVEN FOR EACH    2831 1451
        PRODUCT.  COMPARES WELL WITH P EMISSION DATA WHEN COMBINED2831 1451
        WITH 6/28.                                                2831 1451
  6-107 (N,A) REACTION; INCLUDES SIMPLE CONSTANT YIELDS FOR A     2831 1451
        AND 57FE RESIDUAL, AND ENERGY DEPENDENT YIELD BASED       2831 1451
        ON CALCULATED GAMMA-RAY SPECTRA FOR GAMMA RAY;            2831 1451
        CALCULATED NORMALIZED DISTRIBUTIONS ARE GIVEN FOR EACH    2831 1451
        PRODUCT.  COMPARES WELL WITH A EMISSION DATA WHEN COMBINED2831 1451
        WITH 6/22.                                                2831 1451
 12-51 THROUGH 12-61 BRANCHING RATIOS FOR THE LEVELS, COMPILED    2831 1451
        BY HETRICK ET AL. (5), ARE GIVEN.                         2831 1451
 12-102 (N,G) CAPTURE; MULTIPLICITIES WERE TNG CALCULATED.        2831 1451
 14-51 THROUGH 14-58 AND 14-102 GAMMA RAY ANGULAR DISTRIBUTIONS   2831 1451
        ASSUMED TO BE ISOTROPIC.                                  2831 1451
 15-102 (N,G) CAPTURE; TNG CALCULATED                             2831 1451
                                                                  2831 1451
--------------------------------------------------------------    2831 1451
            UNCERTAINTY FILES                                     2831 1451
        AN LB=8 SECTION IS INCLUDED FOR ALL NON-DERIVED FILES AS  2831 1451
        REQUIRED BY ENDF/B-VI.                                    2831 1451
                                                                  2831 1451
 33-1   UNCERTAINTIES ARE DERIVED FROM 1.E-5 TO 100 EV.  FROM 100 2831 1451
        EV TO 20 MEV THEY ARE EXPLICIT, USING LB=0,1 AND 8.       2831 1451
 33-2   FROM 1.E-5 TO 100 EV, UNCERTAINTIES ARE EXPLICIT, BASED   2831 1451
        UPON THERMAL UNCERTAINTY AND OTHER DATA.  FROM 100 EV TO  2831 1451
        20 MEV THE FILES ARE DERIVED.                             2831 1451
 33-3   FROM 1.E-5 TO 450 KEV UNCERTAINTIES ARE DERIVED.  FROM 4502831 1451
        KEV TO 20 MEV UNCERTAINTIES ARE EXPLICIT, USING LB=1 AND 82831 1451
 33-4   UNCERTAINTIES ARE ALL DERIVED.                            2831 1451
 33-16  COVARIANCES WERE ESTIMATED AS NO DATA AVAILABLE.          2831 1451
 33-22  UNCERTAINTIES FOR (N,NA) ARE EXPLICIT, ESTIMATED FROM TNG 2831 1451
 33-28  UNCERTAINTIES FOR (N,NP) ARE EXPLICIT, ESTIMATED FROM DATA2831 1451
        AND CALCULATION.                                          2831 1451
 33-51-91  UNCERTAINTIES FOR INELASTIC SCATTERING ARE EXPLICIT,   2831 1451
           BASED ON DATA AND CALCULATION UNCERTAINTIES.           2831 1451
 33-102 UNCERTAINTIES ARE EXPLICIT, BASED ON THERMAL DATA AT LOW  2831 1451
        ENERGIES, AND CALCULATED RESULTS ABOVE 450 KEV.           2831 1451
 33-103 COVARIANCES - DATA OF VONACH ET AL. (10) AND CSISRS DATA  2831 1451
        USED AS A GUIDE.                                          2831 1451
 33-104 UNCERTAINTIES ESTIMATED, BASED ON DATA                    2831 1451
 33-107 UNCERTAINTIES EXPLICIT, BASED ON DATA AND TNG RESULTS.    2831 1451
